{"ld": 647, "paper": "HP415", "session": "132", "title": "An Act Regarding Telephone and Video Call Access in Detention and Correctional Facilities and Jails", "sponsor_id": "h-milliken-nina", "cosponsor_ids": ["h-bishop-steven", "h-boyer-david", "s-carney-anne", "h-fredericks-ann", "h-guerrette-timothy", "h-mathieson-kristi", "h-sargent-holly", "h-sayre-daniel", "h-warren-sophia"], "committee_code": "CJPS", "committee_name": "Criminal Justice and Public Safety", "summary": {"text": "This bill amends the laws governing telephone services for residents of detention and correctional facilities and jails to include video call services. For a detention or correctional facility administered by the Department of Corrections, it requires the department to provide a resident a telephone and video call allowance for 90 minutes of free telephone and video calls per week. The department also must provide a resident free telephone and video calls with the resident's attorney. A service provider may not charge a fee to deposit money into a resident's telephone or video call account. For a municipal or county jail, it requires the sheriff or jailer to provide a resident with a reasonable opportunity to make telephone and video calls to relatives and friends, except that the sheriff or jailer may restrict or prohibit telephone and video calls when the restriction or prohibition is necessary for the security of the jail. The sheriff or jailer must provide to a resident who has less than $50 in the resident's jail account a telephone and video call allowance for 90 minutes of 1502 free telephone and video calls per week. The sheriff or jailer also must provide a resident 1513 with a reasonable opportunity to make telephone and video calls protected by the attorney- 1524 client privilege. The sheriff or jailer must provide a resident free telephone and video calls 1535 with the resident's attorney. The bill specifies requirements for service providers regarding 1546 outgoing interstate and intrastate telephone and video calls.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0415&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "died", "status_label": "Accepted Majority (ONTP) Report", "final_disposition": {"label": "Accepted Majority (ONTP) Report", "date": "2025-06-10", "governor_action": null, "governor_action_date": null}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "fiscal_note_url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/bills_132nd/fiscalpdfs/FN064702.pdf", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 647)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0415&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (H-599)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0415&item=2&snum=132", "item": 2}], "amendments": [{"id": "C-A (H-599)", "description": "Change Title", "sponsor": null, "status": null, "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0415&item=2&snum=132", "fiscal_note_url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/bills_132nd/fiscalpdfs/FN064702.pdf"}], "committee_actions": [{"date": "2025-05-01", "action": "Work Session Held", "result": null}, {"date": "2025-05-01", "action": "Voted", "result": "Divided Report"}, {"date": "2025-06-09", "action": "Reported Out", "result": "ONTP/OTP-AM"}], "committee_reports": [{"label": "Majority report", "recommendation": "Ought Not To Pass", "signer_count": 7, "signers": ["Representative Tavis Hasenfus (Chair)", "Representative Donald Ardell", "Senator Scott Cyrway", "Representative Michel Lajoie", "Representative Mathew McIntyre", "Representative Robert Nutting", "Representative Chad Perkins"], "signer_ids": ["h-hasenfus-tavis", "h-ardell-donald", "s-cyrway-scott", "h-lajoie-michel", "h-mcintyre-mathew", "h-nutting-robert", "h-perkins-chad"]}, {"label": "Minority report", "recommendation": "Ought To Pass As Amended", "signer_count": 4, "signers": ["Representative Mana Abdi", "Representative 